      "writtenOn": "2021-10-01T19:03:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still think this can be handled by ioex_init().  But change the new flag name to IOEX_FLAGS_INITIALIZED.\n\nIOEX_FLAGS_INITIALIZED is initialized to zero for all ports.\n\nIf pre-task calls ioex_init(), the port is initialized, and the IOEX_FLAGS_INITIALIZED flag gets set.\n\nWhen ioex_init_default() is called during normal startup, ioex_init() is called on all ports unconditionally.  ioex_init() returns EC_SUCCESS for any ports initialized during pre-task.\n\nThis way, the board code only needs to call ioex_init() for the ports it needs, and the board code doesn\u0027t also have to also set IOEX_FLAGS_PRE_TASK_INITIALIZED flag.",
